# Shell scripts must stay LF even in a Windows working tree.
#
# This team develops on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF. A `#!/bin/sh` script with CRLF endings does not execute — the
# interpreter is read as "/bin/sh\r" and the hook dies with "bad interpreter", or
# silently misbehaves. Pinning the ending here fixes it for every clone instead of
# depending on each machine's git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/** text eol=lf
